 (REPORT/"figure_2A_interpretation.md").write_text("# Figure 2A interpretation\n\nCircadian matching raises raw shared-neighbor counts because two-hour pools are smaller. Chance adjustment substantially reduces this mechanical increase. Clinical-to-h0 remains the strongest preserved comparison. Adjusted purity is highest in clinical space, smaller in h0, and near chance in ht; uncertainty is greatest for insulin-dependent participants.\n")
 positive=did[(did.ci_low>0)]; residual="Positive residual dynamic effects were supported for: "+", ".join(SL[r.canonical_stratum]+" "+ML[r.dynamic_metric] for r in positive.itertuples()) if len(positive) else "No dynamic difference-in-differences interval supported a positive residual night effect after subtracting the static control."
 (REPORT/"figure_2B_interpretation.md").write_text("# Figure 2B interpretation\n\nDay and night estimates use paired participants. Clinical-to-h0 is static, so its night-day difference is a candidate-pool or composition effect rather than streaming physiology. "+residual+" Insulin-dependent estimates are exploratory.\n")
 (REPORT/"STEP2_RECREATED_FIGURES_INTERPRETATION.md").write_text("# Step 2 recreated figures interpretation\n\n## Metric clarification\n\nSelected subtype-specific k values are 11, 8, 9, and 8. Shared count is the set intersection; shared fraction divides by effective k; Jaccard divides by the union. Chance-adjusted overlap subtracts the candidate-pool-matched null and rescales by one minus expected overlap. Adjusted purity uses frozen-label permutations preserving pool prevalence.\n\n## Effect of circadian matching\n\nTwo-hour matching increases raw overlap because it reduces candidate pools. Participant-paired, chance-adjusted results remain directionally consistent for the strongest Clinical-to-h0 structure but are substantially smaller than raw Jaccard suggests.\n\n## Clinical-label organization\n\nAdjusted purity is positive in clinical space, weaker in h0, and approximately chance-level in ht. The Clinical > h0 > ht ordering is most consistent in the mean estimates; h0 and ht intervals are uncertain in several subtypes.\n\n## Day versus night\n\nRaw overlap is higher at night, but the static Clinical-to-h0 control also changes. "+residual+" The smaller insulin-dependent sample limits precision.\n\n## Final conclusion\n\nCircadian matching indicates partial preservation rather than complete reorganization. Candidate-pool composition explains part of the raw night increase. Remaining adjusted differences are residual associations, not direct physiological effects.\n")
 qa=["Exact overlap formula documented","Shared count and Jaccard separated","Both figures use chance-adjusted shared fraction","Elapsed times labeled as 6, 12, 24, 48 h","Matched and unmatched use the same participant anchors after alignment","Day-night inference is paired","Pool sizes saved and displayed","Overlap null preserves effective k and pool size","Purity null preserves cluster prevalence","Clinical-to-h0 labeled static negative control","Raw purity accompanied by chance adjustment","Day-night interpretation uses difference-in-differences","Insulin-dependent explicitly exploratory","Error bars centered on estimates","Existing figures unchanged","All plotted values saved","Old-scale discrepancy explained"]
 (QA/"STEP2_FIGURE_RECREATION_QA_REPORT.md").write_text("# Step 2 figure recreation QA report\n\n"+"\n".join(f"{i}. PASS: {x}" for i,x in enumerate(qa,1))+"\n\nThe Step 2 neighborhood figures were recreated using an explicit shared-neighbor metric, candidate-pool-matched permutation nulls, chance-adjusted purity, paired unmatched-versus-matched comparisons, and direct paired night-minus-day contrasts. Existing figures, hidden states, frozen clinical labels, selected k, and model checkpoints were not modified.\n")
